    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.align\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nThis one is really weird, the align with preview (doesn't happen with the non preview one) prompt in the message bar disappears after a short (maybe 250ms) delay, and is replaced with the `-- VISUAL LINE --` message when started in that mode, works fine in other modes. And only if there is an LSP server attached to the buffer.\n\nHaven't noticed the same thing happening with any other plugin or mini module. Only in this extremely specific mini.align situation.\n\nSpent a solid hour disabling all of my plugins before I spotted the pattern.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nWas able to repro it with this minimal config, with lua_ls as the LSP server of choice, but tested with other servers too, it's not isolated to it specifically:\n```lua\n-- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\nvim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\nlocal clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim', mini_path }\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\nvim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n-- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\nvim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\nrequire('mini.deps').setup()\nrequire('mini.align').setup()\n\nMiniDeps.add('neovim/nvim-lspconfig')\nMiniDeps.now(function()\n    vim.lsp.enable('lua_ls')\nend)\n```\n\nWith that config, and of course lua_ls installed, open any lua file, go into visual line mode and press gA after selecting a few lines to see the issue. ",
