            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThis is not really an issue with 'mini.align', but how Neovim works when there is something shown in the command line. If there is a redraw (i.e. `:redraw` or `vim.api.nvim__redraw()` is executed) and 'showmode' is enabled, then the mode is forced to be shown.\n\nIt can be verified by executing something like `:lua vim.defer_fn(function() vim.cmd.redraw() end, 5000)` (schedule redraw in 5 seconds) and immediately doing something like `VipgA`. After about 5 seconds the prompt from 'mini.align' is replaced with '-- VISUAL LINE --`, while pressing keys afterwards shows 'mini.align' state again.\n\nThe attached LSP server seems to just have forced redraw at some fixed debounced/throttled rate.\n\nI am afraid I don't think there is much 'mini.align' can do here. It can completely change how preview state is shown, but it is a bit overkill. It can maybe also force showing message after every redraw with `vim.api.nvim_set_decoration_provider()`, but it doesn't work cleanly (because decoration providers are not really meant for this sort of thing).\n\nAt this point, I think the best approach to resolve this is to document that preview works best with `vim.o.showmode = false`.",
