            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Yeah, that's what I suspected, the reason why I reported it here is because it's the only plugin I have seen have issue with it, for example flash.nvim doesn't seem to get overwritten even when launched from the same mode. Though that might be that I just got lucky and all my other plugins decided to go for the overkill route.\n\n`vim.o.showmode = false` is probably a good enough fix for me, as I don't really use that bit of the UI anyway. Just a bit of a shame that's the best solution we have.",
