            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> ... for example flash.nvim doesn't seem to get overwritten even when launched from the same mode.\n\n'folke/flash.nvim' doesn't use command line to show information. In the same way as 'mini.jump2d' doesn't have any issues with 'showmode'.\n\n> `vim.o.showmode = false` is probably a good enough fix for me, as I don't really use that bit of the UI anyway. Just a bit of a shame that's the best solution we have.\n\nThe 'noshowmode' is the \"suggested\" setting anyway in 'mini.nvim' (it is set in 'mini.basics', for example), mostly because it is indeed redundant with most of statuslines (like 'mini.statusline', but not only).",
